  crates/profile/src/lib.rs
      The qbt profile's announce parameter set and order, percent-encoding
      rules (escape_string.cpp) and peer-id tail alphabet (string_util.cpp,
      url_random) were transcribed from the oracle's captures and confirmed
      against libtorrent 2.0.14 (http_tracker_connection.cpp).
  crates/tracker/src/announcer.rs
      Tier selection, event sequencing and failure backoff follow
      libtorrent's torrent.cpp (announce_with_tracker) and
      announce_entry.cpp (failed()).
  crates/wire/src/fast.rs
      The unmasked-address allowed-fast set (Q7) follows
      bt_peer_connection::send_allowed_set.
  crates/session/src/engine/pex.rs
      PEX cadence, eligibility, flags and flood limits follow ut_pex.cpp.
  crates/session/src/engine/metadata.rs
      Metadata request scheduling, penalties and serving limits follow
      ut_metadata.cpp.
  crates/session/src/engine/lsd.rs, crates/tracker/src/lsd.rs
      Datagram layout, multicast setup and retry schedule follow lsd.cpp;
      the session round-robin follows session_impl.cpp (on_lsd_announce).
  crates/wire/src/priority.rs
      BEP 40 canonical priority masking follows torrent_peer.cpp
      (peer_priority).
  crates/wire/src/conn.rs
      The deferred allowed-fast set (on `interested`, skipping the peer's
      pieces) follows peer_connection.cpp (send_allowed_set) and the
      have-state rules bt_peer_connection.cpp (write_bitfield, on_metadata).
  crates/dht/src/id.rs, node.rs, table.rs, storage.rs, token.rs, blocker.rs, krpc.rs
      The DHT node ports libtorrent's kademlia implementation: node_id.cpp
      (BEP 42 generation / verification, secret ids), routing_table.cpp
      (bucket layout, replacement cache, split / refresh policy),
      traversal_algorithm.cpp, get_peers.cpp, find_data.cpp, refresh.cpp,
      rpc_manager.cpp and node.cpp (lookups, bootstrap, refresh, request
      handling and reply shapes), dht_storage.cpp (peer store limits, BEP 33
      filters, BEP 51 samples), dos_blocker.cpp.
  crates/session/src/engine/dht.rs
      The announce round-robin follows session_impl.cpp (on_dht_announce).
  crates/utp/src/socket.rs, manager.rs, packet_buffer.rs, history.rs
      The uTP implementation ports libtorrent's utp_stream.cpp (LEDBAT
      congestion control, slow start, RTT / timeout estimation, loss and
      fast-resend handling, nagle, selective acks, close reason, path-MTU
      discovery, the close handshake), utp_socket_manager.cpp (connection
      ids, SYN acceptance, deferred acks, MTU restriction), packet_buffer.cpp
      (the sequence-number-indexed ring), timestamp_history.cpp and
      sliding_average.hpp.
  crates/session/src/engine/peer.rs
      The uTP-first transport choice and the TCP fallback after a failed uTP
      dial follow torrent.cpp (connect_to_peer), torrent_peer.cpp
      (supports_utp) and peer_connection.cpp (on_connection_complete,
      on_connect_timeout); the close reason codes follow close_reason.hpp.
  crates/picker/src/lib.rs
      Piece extent affinity (extent size, the five recent extents, when an
      extent is recorded) follows piece_picker.cpp
      (record_downloading_piece, pick_pieces).
  crates/session/src/engine/external_ip.rs
      External-address voting (vote filtering, rotation thresholds) follows
      ip_voter.cpp; the listen-port decision follows session_impl.cpp
      (listen_port(ssl, local_addr)).
